{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-5 are wired through the same SDK/CLI production path and both required gates pass, but Story 1's thread-creation contract has an untested edge that breaks every later story by registering a thread with no durable file.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The domain/import structure matches the tech-design layout and the boundary gate passed: `boundaries: OK (38 files checked, fixtures exempt)`.\",\"Thread creation does not validate non-empty paths at the SDK boundary; `newThread({ filePath: \\\"\\\" })` reaches `node:sqlite`, which opens a temporary database, then inserts a registry row for `filePath: \\\"\\\"`.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"The implemented tests cover the epic TC table broadly: `verify-all` reported 16 files and 111 tests passing.\",\"Coverage is missing for invalid empty thread file paths on `threads.newThread` and the CLI `threads new-thread --file-path ''` path, so AC-1.1/AC-1.3/AC-1.4 are not fully proven.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material fake adapter, shim, or placeholder execution path was found in the accepted intake, projection, turn, or work-queue flow; the stale `notImplemented` helper is present but unused by production commands.\",\"Material production-path defect: the real SDK and real built CLI can create a registry row for an empty path without creating a thread file. Exact observed CLI sequence: `threads new-thread --file-path ''` returned `{ ok: true, value: { threadId: \\\"th_0fea4c8735507259\\\", filePath: \\\"\\\" } }`; `threads resolve` returned that row; `intake-stream list-events --thread-id th_0fea4c8735507259` then returned `{ ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\", code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\", reason: \\\"no thread file exists at \\\" } }`.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-EPIC-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Thread creation accepts an empty path and registers a non-existent thread file\",\"evidence\":\"`packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/index.ts:73` only checks `existsSync(input.filePath)` before `createThreadFile`. Node's `DatabaseSync(\\\"\\\")` succeeds as a temporary database, so `newThread({ filePath: \\\"\\\" })` returned `ok: true` with `filePath: \\\"\\\"`, no file existed at that path, and the registry still resolved the generated thread id to `\\\"\\\"`. The built CLI reproduced the same behavior with `threads new-thread --file-path ''`, after which `intake-stream list-events --thread-id <id>` failed with `thread_not_found`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-1.4\",\"TC-1.1\",\"TC-1.6\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-EPIC-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Some read-back CLI commands do not enforce the required thread reference flags\",\"evidence\":\"`packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts:176` through `packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts:183` call `messages.list`, `messages.list-queued-work`, `turns.list`, and `turns list-queued-work` without the missing `--thread-id`/`--file-path` guard used by intake commands. Running `node packages/lhc/dist/cli.js messages list` returned `thread_not_found` for an empty path instead of a usage/missing-flag error.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/projection.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/turns.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"CLI conventions\",\"AC-1.6\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
